  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Vertical component of velocity, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Time taken to reach the highest point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> Time taken to reach the ground from highest point.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>At the highest point, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> splits up into two parts of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math></p><p>If their velocities are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively, then applying the principle of conservation of linear momentum, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Initial <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>Final <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;(initial <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></math>)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Solving Eq. (i) and (ii), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the separation between the two fragments</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
  }
}